<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43246" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sectĭlĭs</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		seco. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Cut</i>, <i>cleft</i>, <i>divided</i>, etc. (not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ebur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Med.
					Fac. 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lamnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 43, 83, § 226</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pavimenta,</span>”
				<i>made of small cut stones</i>, <i>mosaic</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
					1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 46 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That may be cut</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porrum,</span>”
				<i>cut-leek</i>, <i>chives</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					3, 293</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 48, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 24, 11</span></i> (cf. sectivus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 22, 44, § 159</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medulla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 39, 76, § 195</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tuber,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 43, 84, § 231</span></i>
			.</div>
